title: No runtime fallback
tags: Configuration [[Key invariants]]
kind: reference
summary: A missing or malformed configuration file, or a missing setting, stops the program with a message naming it; no program keeps its defaults in its code.

No program keeps its defaults in its code: they live only in the files
`metafolder-sync-config` installs. A missing file, a missing setting or a malformed
file is reported, naming it and the problem, and the program stops. It never falls back
to a built-in default — the canonical one may have been deleted on purpose.

Only what has no default may be left out — `[[load]]`, `[repo]` — and `memory-dir`,
whose default holds your uid, which a shipped file cannot spell. So a key you remove to
"go back to the default" stops the program: restore it with
`git checkout default -- <file>` ([[Updating the configuration]]). A new key arrives
with the merge of a new version; while a merge stays in conflict, a program that needs
that key refuses to start until it is resolved.

|!File |!Read by |!Missing |!Malformed |
|`core/query-grammar` |the GUI at startup, `mf` with `-s` — never the daemon |error when loaded |error when loaded; an ''empty'' file is one, having no `query` production |
|`core/ignore-presets.toml` |`mf ignore`, `mf repo init`, the GUI's repository creation — never the daemon |error when loaded (`mf repo init --no-ignore` skips it) |error |
|`gui/config.toml`, `gui/keybindings.toml` |the GUI; `mf gui` reads `gui-port` of `gui/config.toml` unless `--gui-url` names the GUI |error at startup; `mf gui`: error, exit 2 |error at startup; `mf gui`: error, exit 2 |
|`gui/style.css` |the GUI |error at startup |nothing checks it: the WebView ignores what it cannot parse |
|`gui/commands.js`, `gui/user-commands.js`, `gui/macros.js` |the GUI; the WebView imports them |error at startup |shown on screen, and the UI does not appear; on `config:reload commands`, in the status bar, the commands already installed staying |
|`gui/command-classes.toml` |the GUI, at startup and each time the [[keybindings panel]] reads it |error at startup; afterwards the panel shows the error and the commands unclassed |same as missing |
|`daemon/config.toml` |the daemon |error at startup |error at startup |
|`cli/config.toml` |`mf`, or the file `--config` names |error, exit 2, before any daemon call |error, exit 2, before any daemon call |
|`daemon/repo-default/` |`mf repo init`, the GUI's repository creation, `mf repo update-config` — never the daemon |error: no repository is created ([[Repository configuration]]) |copied as it is; the repository's load then reports it |
|a repository's `config/metadata-map.toml` |the daemon, at the repository's load |error: that repository does not load ([[The metadata map]]) |error: that repository does not load |

A key of `[panel-defaults.<panel>]` is the panel's: the GUI cannot know it, so it is the
panel that stops, on the read of a missing key or on a value it cannot use, and shows
the error while the rest of the GUI goes on ([[GUI configuration]]).

`mf --config FILE` reads that file instead of yours, for scripts that must not depend
on your personal settings.

The normal query language needs no grammar, and works without `core/query-grammar`
([[Editing the grammar]]).
